UWA Honours Thesis – Supplementary Materials - TRUNG HO HUYNH
Project Overview

This repository contains the supplementary materials associated with an Honours thesis investigating the formation processes of grinding-patch cross-sectional morphology through controlled experimentation. The project focuses on understanding how grinding duration and active-stone contact area influence surface morphological change on granite substrates.

Repository Contents
1. Experimental Data
DEMs.zip

This archive contains Digital Elevation Models (DEMs) generated from photogrammetric reconstruction of granite passive stone surfaces.

Derived from close-range photogrammetry using Agisoft Metashape
Exported as TIFF raster files
Represent surface morphology at 20-minute intervals across each experimental run
Used for quantitative terrain analysis (slope calculation)

These DEMs form the primary dataset for analysing surface morphological change over time.

Speed_of_motor_in_experiment_1.zip

This file contains recorded motor performance data from the experimental apparatus.

Includes RPM measurements recorded at 0.1-second intervals
Used to calculate stroke counts and ensure consistency of grinding motion
Provides a quantitative record of experimental control conditions

This dataset supports the internal validity of the experiment by documenting mechanical consistency.

Machine_working_video.zip

This archive contains video documentation of the experimental apparatus in operation.

Shows the mechanical grinding system in use
Demonstrates controlled reciprocal motion
Documents experimental setup and procedure

This serves as visual verification and methodological transparency, allowing replication and evaluation of the experimental design.

2. Analytical Outputs
markdown_statistic_supplyment.html

This file contains the statistical analysis outputs derived from the experimental data.

Generated using R / RMarkdown
Includes regression analysis, correlation tests, and model outputs
Documents relationships between grinding duration, contact area, and surface morphology

This file supports the quantitative interpretation presented in the thesis.

surface_code_for_analysis.R

This script contains the R code used to process and analyse the dataset.

Performs terrain analysis (slope calculation from DEMs)
Computes Mean Surface Index (MSI)
Runs statistical models (correlation tests and linear mixed-effects models)

This ensures reproducibility of all analytical results.
